Question: A specialty chemical factory produces three premium products (A, B, C) by blending three raw materials (1, 2, 3). The factory supplies custom formulations to high-end manufacturers:

Product A is a precision industrial lubricant requiring ≥50% Material 1 and ≤25% Material 2
Product B is an aerospace-grade adhesive requiring ≥25% Material 1 and ≤50% Material 2
Product C is a general-purpose compound with no material restrictions
Raw material costs and availability are in raw_materials.csv, while product specifications and selling prices are in products.csv. Determine the optimal blending plan to maximize daily profit.
